{
  "opening": "This release introduces several critical updates to the humanize library, focusing on type safety, bug fixes, and new functionality. It ensures that public APIs are correctly typed for modern Python environments and resolves edge cases in existing functions like `intcomma` and `naturaldelta`. Additionally, a new `metric` function is added to handle SI unit formatting with specific spacing rules.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The following public names must be exposed exactly as listed: Unit, abs_timedelta, date_and_delta, deactivate, gettext, gettext_noop, intword, naturaldate, naturaldelta, naturaltime, ngettext, ngettext_noop, num_name, pgettext, precisedelta, thousands_separator."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The naturaldelta function must support years in its output when appropriate. The precisedelta function must also correctly handle year-level precision in its formatted output."
    },
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "The naturaldelta function must not overflow or raise errors when handling very large time deltas. The naturaltime function must similarly handle large time deltas without overflow issues."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The following public names must have correct type hints applied: Unit, activate, apnumber, clamp, deactivate, fractional, get_translation, intcomma, intword, naturaldate, naturalday, naturaldelta, naturalsize, naturaltime, ordinal, precisedelta, scientific."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "The metric function must append the unit after the SI prefix with no space between them if the unit is the degree sign, otherwise with a space. For example, metric(1, 'Hz') returns '1.00 Hz', metric(-1500, 'V') returns '-1.50 kV', metric(3, 'W', 5) returns '3.0000 W', and metric(1, '°') returns '1.00°'."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The intcomma function must correctly handle the ndigits parameter when set to 0, ensuring proper formatting without decimal places."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all changes are verified against the existing test suite and that the new metric function behaves exactly as described in the findings."
}
